I think it's safe to say most of us have that one friend, the one who always has their nose in a book, who's way too into their own little world to even notice you're talking to them. They're the type you don't really get to know, more like an acquaintances you cross and wave to as you rush past, or just ignore altogether. 

I was one of these "not easily noticed" people. I was always in my own head, lost in the pages of my book by my 11-year-old self. For the most part, it's not like I'm a bad person, I just go through my life by a totally different set of numbers than everyone out there.

One day, I'm reading a fantasy about a dragon who can speak with anyone and I realize my own voice doesn’t come from me at all. It’s not really even a "real" speaking;
